<title>MOROCCO: Morocco issues Treasury bonds.</title>
<headline>Morocco issues Treasury bonds.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's central bank said on Monday it would issue treasury bonds each valued at 5,000 and 50,000 dirhams.</p>
<p>The bank said subscriptions would be open, with no volume specified, from June 30 to July 3, and that interest rates would be eight percent for one year, 8.5 percent for three years and nine percent for five years.</p>
<p>The central bank issues treasury bonds four times a year. The last issue dating back to March this year raised 390.5 million dirhams.</p>
<p>The bank last week said it had cut interest rates on short and medium-term treasury bills by 0.5 percent to between 8.0 and 9.0 percent.</p>
<p>The next issue will be in September, a bank spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>($ = 9.5 dirhams)</p>
